---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import PageTitle from "../components/PageTitle.astro";
import LinkButton from "../components/LinkButton.astro";
---

<Page title="Archive" description="The LSQ archive: every story, every issue, going back to 2010">
  <PageTitle title="The LSQ Archive" />


  <p class="mb-2">
    Luna Station Quarterly has been publishing speculative fiction by women-identified authors since
    2010. 
  </p>
  <p class="mb-2">
    For a long time the archive was open and free online. Then AI companies started scraping the
    internet for training data, and our authors' work was sitting there exposed. We took it down to
    protect them. Getting it back up took longer than we wanted, but it's back now in a
    members-only space where the stories are safe.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6">
    The archive is online reading only, which makes it a great option if you don't do ebooks.
    Access is available as long as your subscription is active. A new passcode is posted with each
    quarterly issue release.
  </p>

  <hr class="border-lsq-gray-light mb-6" />

  <h2 class="font-normal font-sans text-3xl m-0 pb-4">How to Access the Archive</h2>

  <p class="mb-4">You've got two options.</p>

  <h3 class="font-normal font-sans text-2xl m-0 pb-3">Patreon</h3>
  <p class="mb-3">
    Patreon includes archive access plus everything else: digital editions of new issues, exclusive
    posts, and access to the LSQ community. If you want to be part of what we're building here,
    this is the place.
  </p>
  <ul class="mb-4 marker:text-lsq-black">
    <li>Station Resident ($1/mo): Current issue</li>
    <li>Station Crew ($5/mo): Current issue plus the last three (a full year)</li>
    <li>Station Lorekeeper ($10/mo): Full archive back to 2010</li>
    <li>Command Crew ($15/mo): Full archive plus print</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="mb-6">
    <LinkButton url="https://patreon.com/lunastation" linkText="Join on Patreon" />
  </div>

  <h3 class="font-normal font-sans text-2xl m-0 pb-3">Payhip</h3>
  <p class="mb-3">
    Payhip is online-only archive access, no extras. If you just want the stories, this works
    great.
  </p>
  <ul class="mb-3 marker:text-lsq-black">
    <li>Station Resident ($3/quarter): Current issue</li>
    <li>Station Crew ($12/quarter): Current issue plus the last three</li>
    <li>Station Lorekeeper ($25/quarter): Full archive back to 2010</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-4 italic text-lsq-gray">Note: Command Crew (print) is Patreon-only.</p>
  <div class="mb-6">
    <LinkButton url="https://payhip.com/b/Pu7eM" linkText="Join on Payhip" />
  </div>

  <hr class="border-lsq-gray-light mb-6" />

  <h2 class="font-normal font-sans text-3xl m-0 pb-4">What's in the Archive</h2>

  <p class="mb-2">
    65+ issues. 900+ stories. Fifteen years of speculative fiction by women-identified authors:
    science fiction, fantasy, space opera, fairy tales, weird fiction, and everything in between.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6">We publish four times a year. The archive grows with every issue.</p>

  <hr class="border-lsq-gray-light mb-6" />

  <h2 class="font-normal font-sans text-3xl m-0 pb-4">Questions</h2>

  <p class="mb-6">
    Check the FAQ below, or use our <a href="/contact-us">contact form</a> if you need something
    we haven't covered.
  </p>

  <dl class="space-y-6">
    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">How do I access the archive?</dt>
      <dd>
        When you subscribe, you'll receive a passcode that unlocks the archive site. The passcode
        is posted with each new issue release on both Payhip and Patreon. You'll need an active
        subscription to receive it.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">Does the passcode change?</dt>
      <dd>
        Yes, every time a new issue comes out (four times a year). As long as your subscription is
        active, you'll have access to the updated passcode when it's posted.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">What format are the issues in?</dt>
      <dd>
        The archive is online reading only. No downloads or ebook files. This makes it a great
        option for readers who prefer not to manage ebook libraries.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">What happens if I cancel my subscription?</dt>
      <dd>
        Your access ends when your subscription lapses. You won't receive future passcodes after
        canceling.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">I'm a Station Resident. What happens when a new issue comes out?</dt>
      <dd>
        The current issue rotates with each new release. When a new issue publishes, the previous
        one is no longer included in your tier.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">How many issues are in the archive?</dt>
      <dd>
        65+ issues going back to 2010, with over 900 stories. Station Lorekeeper members get
        access to all of it.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">Can I switch from Payhip to Patreon?</dt>
      <dd>
        Yes! Patreon membership includes everything on Payhip plus digital editions, exclusive
        posts, and access to the LSQ community. You can join Patreon anytime and cancel your
        Payhip subscription when you're ready.{" "}
        
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">Can I upgrade my tier?</dt>
      <dd>Yes, anytime.</dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">Can I share my passcode?</dt>
      <dd>
        We operate on the honor system here. LSQ is a small independent publication run mostly by
        volunteers, and subscriptions are what keep it going. If you love the archive, the best
        thing you can do is encourage the people in your life to subscribe too.
      </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
      <dt class="font-bold mb-1">What's the difference between Payhip and Patreon?</dt>
      <dd>
        Both support LSQ directly. Payhip is straightforward online-only archive access. Patreon
        costs a little more but gives you a lot more: digital editions, exclusive posts, and access
        to the LSQ community. It's also where you'll find our Editor In Chief, Jennifer Lyn Parsons.
        
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</Page>
